See test.desc.  No longer a crash: the diagnostic "base class ... is
incomplete" is issued, but ill-formed implicit instantiations of user class
templates are tolerated in general ([temp.inst]: the front end keeps going
with a degenerate instance), so the program is accepted.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 reject it.
